  "final_message": "I haven't removed `channel`, because doing that would break ARCH-4.\n\n`OrderPlaced` (`src/core/events.ts:16`, schemaVersion 3) is consumed by billing-service and analytics-ingest, which live in other repos. ARCH-4 says no change may break a deployed consumer, and that removals must go through deprecation. Nothing in this repo reads `channel`, but I can't see whether those two services do. Dropping it from the payload is a breaking change. The order model feeds both the event and the HTTP responses, so I'd also check ARCH-8 (`GET /orders/{id}` must stay backward compatible) before touching it.\n\nThere are three ways to go:\n\n1. **Deprecate first (my recommendation).**\n   - Mark `channel` as `@deprecated` on the event.\n   - Make it optional on `POST /orders` and in `createOrder`, so new callers don't have to send it.\n   - Keep publishing it, with a default value when the caller omits it, until billing-service and analytics-ingest confirm they don't read it.\n   - Remove it afterwards, as a new schema version.\n2. **Confirm the consumers first.** If you already know or can check that both services ignore `channel`, tell me. I'll still suggest a schema version bump, but I can then remove it from the event, the order model, request parsing, validation, tests and docs.\n3. **Internal-only cleanup.** I can remove `channel` from the internal model and from validation, but keep it on the event, which would mean hardcoding a value. I don't think that's worth doing.\n\nWhich one do you want?",
